  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We have a product of a positive number $(5.2)$ and a negative number $(-3).$ So the product will be negative:\n\n$$\n5.2\\cdot (-3)=-\\,\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply $5.2$ by $3$ without any signs: $5.2\\cdot 3=15.6.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n5.2\\cdot (-3)=-15.6.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
